const path = require("path");
const { PrismaClient } = require(path.join("/opt/nxeon", "node_modules/@prisma/client"));
const db = new PrismaClient();

const BOARD_ID = "cmsavfvil000hhla4nlpuyge6";
const COL_ID = "cmsavfvin000khla4anofdbxt"; // In progress

const description = [
"Google Sign-in **and** Sign-up for the customer booking portal (SoulPilates.Astro + SoulPilates.API).",
"Built on the STAGING stack only; committed to branch `feature/google-auth` and pushed to origin. Prod untouched.",
"",
"**What it does**: OAuth 2.0 authorization-code flow. Existing users sign in (matched by verified Google email); first-timers get a new account auto-linked to their CRM Client. Same JWT as the password flow. Ships **dark** (self-gated) until Google creds are set.",
].join("\n");

const comment = `## Google Sign-in & Sign-up — build complete (staging, dark)

**Branch:** \`feature/google-auth\` (commit 5360d34), pushed to \`origin\` (github.com/santino1233/soulpilatescrm). Prod NOT deployed.

### What was built
**Backend (SoulPilates.API / Services / Core)**
- \`GoogleOAuthService\` — builds the consent URL, exchanges the \`code\` at Google's token endpoint, validates the id_token (aud/iss/exp). No extra NuGet deps.
- \`CustomerAuthService.SignInWithGoogleAsync\` — resolution order: (1) match by stored \`GoogleId\`; (2) match by **verified** email and link Google onto that existing (password) account; (3) create a new account auto-linked to the CRM Client. New Google accounts get an unusable random BCrypt hash + \`AuthProvider="google"\`. Issues the **same JWT** the password login uses.
- \`CustomerAccount\` gained \`GoogleId\` + \`AuthProvider\`.
- \`CustomerAuthController\` — \`GET /api/customer/google/{enabled,start,callback}\` with an HttpOnly CSRF-nonce cookie + open-redirect guard.
- **Account-safety:** Google's \`email_verified\` MUST be true before linking, so an unverified Google email can never hijack a password account. No duplicate accounts (matched by googleId then email).

**Frontend (Astro)**
- "Continue with Google" button on \`/login\` and \`/register\`, styled to the Soul Pilates system, hidden until the backend reports the feature is configured.
- New \`/auth/google\` landing page stores the JWT in localStorage (\`customer_token\` etc.) and lands the user in (new users → /onboarding).

**Self-gate:** with no client id/secret, \`/api/customer/google/start\` returns 404 and the button stays hidden — so it deploys dark and lights up the instant creds are added, no code change.

### Staging verification (https://staging.soulpilates.com.vn)
- Backend booted clean — no IDX10703, "Now listening on :8080".
- \`/api/customer/google/enabled\` → 200 \`{"enabled":false}\` · \`/api/customer/google/start\` → 404 (gated) · \`/api/settings\` → 401. No 500s.
- \`/login\`, \`/register\`, \`/auth/google\` all 200; button HTML + OAuth wiring present in the bundle.
- PROD stayed 200 throughout; all \`soulpilates-prod-*\` containers untouched.

---

## ACTION REQUIRED — Google Cloud Console setup (do this to go live)

1. **console.cloud.google.com** → create/select a project (e.g. "Soul Pilates").
2. **APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen**: User type **External**; app name "Soul Pilates"; support + developer email; **Authorized domain** \`soulpilates.com.vn\`; scopes \`openid\`, \`email\`, \`profile\`. Publish the app (or add yourself as a Test user while in Testing).
3. **APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID** → Application type **Web application**, name "Soul Pilates Web".
   - **Authorized redirect URIs** (exact match, add BOTH):
     - Prod: \`https://soulpilates.com.vn/api/customer/google/callback\`
     - Staging: \`https://staging.soulpilates.com.vn/api/customer/google/callback\`
   - (Optional) Authorized JavaScript origins: \`https://soulpilates.com.vn\`, \`https://staging.soulpilates.com.vn\`.
4. Copy the **Client ID** and **Client secret**.

### Env vars to set
Prod → add to \`/opt/soulpilates/prod.env\`:
\`\`\`
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<client id>
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<client secret>
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://soulpilates.com.vn/api/customer/google/callback
\`\`\`
Staging → add to \`/opt/soulpilates-staging/staging.env\` (same, with the staging redirect URI). The compose files already map \`GoogleAuth__ClientId/ClientSecret/RedirectUri\` from these.

## Prod deploy command
Merge \`feature/google-auth\` → \`main\`, set the three GOOGLE_ vars in \`/opt/soulpilates/prod.env\` (or deploy dark and add later), then on 51.79.226.200:
\`\`\`
cd /opt/soulpilates && scripts/deploy-prod.sh
\`\`\`
(That script checks out main, rebuilds the images, recreates backend+frontend with \`--env-file prod.env\`, and smoke-tests /api/settings.)`;

